# WHY this file exists: this repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so
# without it every checkout rewrites LF to CRLF. `start.sh` is executed by `sh`, which
# treats a trailing CR as part of the shebang and the arguments — a fresh clone on Linux
# would fail to launch with a "bad interpreter" error that names a path that looks right.
# The startup smoke test asserts start.sh has no CRLF; this is what makes that true after
# a clone rather than only in the working tree it was authored in.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
# Same reason, for the two files a linux container reads: a CR in the entrypoint is a
# bad interpreter, and a CR in a Dockerfile RUN line ends up inside the command.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
